# Naming: snake_case only

This repo uses **one** naming style. Read `CODING_STANDARD.md`.

- Folders and files: `course_manager`, `course_manager.jsx`, `admin_screens.js`
- Variables and functions: `course_id`, `get_student_profile`, `handle_submit`
- React components: `Course_Manager` (capital parts, underscores). Never `CourseManager`. Never `course_manager` as a component (React will treat it as HTML).
- Constants: `ADMIN_SCREEN_IDS`
- Our CSS classes and our routes: `hero_landing`, `/admin_dashboard`
- Frontend feature folder name must match the backend feature folder name

Do not introduce kebab-case (`performance-dashboard`) or camelCase (`getStudent`) in our code.

Leave names we do not own:

- React / browser: `useState`, `onClick`, `className`, `setTimeout`, `ResizeObserver`, Intl values like `"2-digit"`
- Packages: `@datapromr/*` imports, prop names (`variant`, `onChange`), routes like `/api/csrf-token`
- Package CSS / DOM classes: `.dpm-dash`, `.dpm-dash__main`, `.dpm-select`, `.ui-field`, `.dpm-login-submit__link`, `.gds-toolbar__search`, `.ub-table-wrap`, `.gff-input` (`@datapromr/*` and `@designdaddy/*`)
- CSS properties: `font-size`
- Tool files: `vite.config.js`

AppShell main padding belongs in `design_system/shell.css` only — never snake_case package shell or DataGrid selectors, and never set `.dpm-dash__main` padding in feature CSS.
